## Why every frame agrees

The oriented area is $\omega(u,v)=u_1v_2-u_2v_1$, while metric area squared is $\Gamma=g(u,u)g(v,v)-g(u,v)^2$. Their exact relation is $\Gamma=(\det g)\omega^2$.

